  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The new `.golangci.yml` uses the v2 format and enables lll at line-length 100, with a comment tying it to the house width. The hook's Go branch follows the existing filter/have/note style: it runs gofmt on only the staged `.go` files, runs golangci-lint on the module, prints a skip notice when either tool is missing, and is gated on Go files being staged, so a commit without Go files still passes. AGENTS.md gains a Go row."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The only changes are the Go config, the hook, an AGENTS.md row and an allowed `[*.go]` tab section in .editorconfig. No workflow was added, the Go sources and other languages' configs were left alone, and the Markdown and YAML opt-outs are unchanged."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply says the check runs only locally and nothing enforces it on PRs. It flags the header's code-quality.yml claim as stale and notes that only tests.yml exists, running go test. It explains why no workflow was added, and it reports what was run and what wasn't (shellcheck and shfmt were not installed). It does not say outright that a contributor without golangci-lint commits unchecked."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.299999999999999
  },
